Package: [[name]]
# Not [[version]]: that is the raw Maven version, and apt compares on this line. This is Sokar's
# version with -SNAPSHOT rewritten to ~SNAPSHOT, which sorts below the release rather than above
# it - the same rule the agent packages follow.
Version: [[sokar.package.version]]
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: fuin.org <info@fuin.org>
Homepage: https://github.com/sokar-ai/sokar
# Podman 5, as the setup script demands: a plain apt install on a release offering 4 would fail 'sokar doctor'.
# The C library and zlib at the floor the binaries were measured to need: jdeb does not read them.
Depends: podman (>= 5), nftables, dnsmasq-base, git, util-linux, libc6 (>= [[package.glibc.floor]]), zlib1g
# Recommended, not required: they depend on sokar, so requiring them would be a cycle. apt installs
# a recommendation by default, which is what a machine without the setup script needs - without the
# filter nothing leaves a task.
Recommends: sokar-message-sluice-filter
Description: [[description]]
 Sandboxes an AI agent task in a hardened, rootless podman container: egress is
 default-deny, credentials stay on the host behind a broker, and the agent hands
 its work back through a git gate the operator reviews.
 .
 Installs the sokar and sokard binaries and the three OCI hooks. The hooks are
 statically linked and are NOT registered by this package: podman reads hook
 descriptors per user, so each operator runs "sokar setup" once, which writes
 them into ~/.config/containers and points podman at them. Nothing here touches
 a system-wide podman configuration.
 .
 Where SELinux is enforcing, a task container cannot reach sokar's sockets until
 the policy module in /usr/share/sokar/selinux is installed. "sokar doctor"
 reports whether it is.
 .
 This package contains no agent. Agents ship separately as sokar-agent-*
 packages, which sokar discovers by scanning /usr/libexec/sokar/agents.
